<title>BELGIUM: Belgian bonds closing report.</title>
<headline>Belgian bonds closing report.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The spread of Belgian linear bonds over Bunds ended at a record low of 15 bp as markets welcomed news of government deal on the 1997 budget, which aims to cut the state deficit to 2.9 percent of GDP from 3.0 in 1996.</p>
<p>The 2006 OLO ended at 6.23 percent, 15 bps over Bunds from 16 at the Thursday close. The spread briefly dipped to 14 bp intraday.</p>
<p>Dealers said most of the good news had been discounted by the market and said there was more downside risk than upside potential for the spread.</p>
